{"card_hash": "48a508be987d1b5655805bb2386648a4c883aad5427226c8bbc973f8afa2b6ba", "channel": "Movez", "chars": 15659, "chars_all_clips": 15659, "chars_chosen_clips": 1440, "clip_count": 10, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/0xMovez/status/2079985963862786352#t=0", "end": 118.659, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "5b15e150df90a0c10541396f215ab7f977a98a5682edba51a961b0b1d4d7d6d7", "start": 0.0, "text": "a little bit about our view of asynchronous agents at Anthropic and some things we've been up to lately. So this is kind of a way I think about models and product so you can think about Clod as a light source and you can think about product", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/0xMovez/status/2079985963862786352#t=118", "end": 236.9, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "08d936e7c87feafea111961f9eeffeb786108a637d072093a20db19d2d8cc3dc", "start": 118.659, "text": "Of deployment with that So you basically take Messages API And roll your own Harness Deploy That Harnish Over the past year We saw The rise Of coding agents In particular So we released Asian sdk So thats Basically A way to Programmatically", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/0xMovez/status/2079985963862786352#t=356", "end": 476.05, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "3a74bb4b657f2ad42c27bc5fe4ac8cf7f4298c53ddb2b26d4e3eedc3b75a3f95", "start": 356.62, "text": "The Problems That We've Seen With Claude In Other Models In General When You Ask Them To Do A Bunch Of Work If That Same Context Is Being Used To Both Do The Work And Grade You Get Lots Of Odd Artifacts In Confabulation And Basically On Beh", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/0xMovez/status/2079985963862786352#t=595", "end": 713.72, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "779c179d0ad23b5ed2953648f18012250d7e628c0b321f90f17b7e416beebd74", "start": 595.08, "text": "Short Term Very Fast Experiential Memory Like Remember What You Had For Lunch Today You Had Lunch An Hour Ago That's Kind Of Written To Short-Term Memory When You Go to Bed At Night Though In Offline Process Or Out of Band Process Dreams An", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/0xMovez/status/2079985963862786352#t=713", "end": 831.919, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "e95bb25680af7775e2acdd9fef702cb411e803b92788e6e0a183888130d28408", "start": 713.72, "text": "Across Models So This Kind Of Showing That Models Get Natively Better At Inband Memory Writing With Respect To Model Capability Some Most Interesting Things I Found From This Are Are That The Main Differentiation Between There You Go The Ma", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/0xMovez/status/2079985963862786352#t=951", "end": 1070.24, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "31e95f285562abcf6df11f742c92044f2d0d43b447aa256ec6c217ba69f3668e", "start": 951.84, "text": "We Release Cloud Tag A Lot Of Reaction Was Like Ah Slackbot And Like Look I Have Actually Created A Lot Of Slackbots Myself Understand Not Every Slackbott Is Particularly Interesting Or Great In Fact I Create Many Slack Bots That Are Quite ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "AI and ML", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/0xMovez/status/2079985963862786352#t=0", "end": 118.659, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "5b15e150df90a0c10541396f215ab7f977a98a5682edba51a961b0b1d4d7d6d7", "start": 0.0, "text": "a little bit about our view of asynchronous agents at Anthropic and some things we've been up to lately. So this is kind of a way I think about models and product so you can think about Clod as a light source and you can think about product", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/0xMovez/status/2079985963862786352#t=118", "end": 236.9, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "0